{:adr-id "2607154500"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-0114 (growing of sugar cane) sugar-cane-plantation-operations-coordination actor"
 :status :accepted
 :date "2026-07-15"
 :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"]
 :related ["ADR-2607122200" "ADR-2607011000" "ADR-2607152600" "ADR-2607152500"]

 :context
 "cloud-itonami-isic-0114 did not exist prior to this ADR (gh api
  repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-0114 returned a GraphQL 404 before
  scaffold) -- a fresh scaffold, not a repair of a prior stray artifact.
  Built from cloud-itonami-isic-0112 (growing of rice) as the
  module-structure template, adapted to sugar cane's perennial,
  ratoon-cropping specifics (ratoon-cycle logging/validation replacing
  0112's paddy water-level check, pre-harvest-burn scheduling and its own
  finalize-burn-decision hard block, borer-pest crop-health concerns),
  with clojure -M:test independently re-run before and after every push."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["direct field-equipment operation (grower's exclusive authority)"
  "finalizing a pre-harvest-burn decision (grower/agronomist authority)"
  "finalizing a pesticide-application decision (agronomist/grower authority)"
  "agronomic decision authority -- what/when/how much to plant, fertilize, burn, harvest (remains human authority)"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-0114 with Governor, Facts, Registry, Store, Advisor,
  Phase, Operation, Sim (mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-0112 module-for-module,
  caneops.* namespace in place of riceops.*):
  - Governor (CaneOperationsGovernor): 6 hard checks (field-not-registered,
    no-execution, equipment-or-decision-blocked [now covers
    :operate-field-equipment, :finalize-burn-decision (NEW), and
    :finalize-pesticide-application], op-not-allowed, field-record-invalid,
    ratoon-cycle-invalid [NEW, perennial-crop-specific]) + 3 escalation gates
    (always-escalate crop-health concern, cost-threshold supply orders,
    low confidence < 0.7)
  - Facts: supply categories with cost thresholds (seed-cane/fertilizer/equipment
    including harvest machinery/irrigation pumps), sugar-cane varieties
    (hybrid/noble/energy-cane/chewing-cane), field-operation-types
    reference set (planting/fertilizing/pre-harvest-burn/harvest/ratooning)
  - Registry: independent pure predicates (cost-exceeds-threshold?,
    acreage-non-positive?, ratoon-cycle-invalid? [NEW], confidence-below-floor?)
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore (registered-field lookup, cane field)
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + MockAdvisor (4 ops, log-field-record now
    also carries :ratoon-cycle, :yield, :brix)
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate
  - Operation: composes advisor -> governor -> phase-gate (langgraph-clj wiring
    deferred, matching 0111/0112's own stub)
  - Sim: demo runner with a working -main
  - Operations: log-field-record, schedule-field-operation,
    flag-crop-health-concern, order-supplies (closed allowlist, :effect :propose)
  - Tests: 35 tests / 107 assertions (facts, governor, phase, registry, store), all green
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop), AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - README/business-model/operator-guide describe the real API, plus a
    dedicated Perennial crop / ratoon-cropping README section"

 :consequences
 {:positive
  ["Sugar-cane growing (0114) now genuinely implemented and fully tested"
   "Scope boundaries (field-equipment operation, pre-harvest-burn decisions,
    pesticide-application decisions) hardcoded in governor checks, not just
    asserted in prose"
   "Crop-health escalation (flag-crop-health-concern, covers borer infestation,
    always human) is a core design invariant"
   "Ratoon-cycle is a first-class, independently validated field (mirrors 0111's
    acreage validation and 0112's water-level validation), reflecting
    ratoon-cropping as sugar cane's operational trait distinguishing it from
    the annual crops covered by its 0111/0112 siblings"
   "Portable .cljc, zero JVM-only constructs, clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings"]
  :negative
  ["Real persistent store (Datomic/kotoba-server) is a follow-up (in-memory for now)"
   "langgraph-clj StateGraph wiring (real interrupt-before/checkpoint resume) is
    deferred scaffolding, matching 0111/0112's own stub status"
   "Brix (sugar-content) is logged as advisor payload data but not independently
    governor-range-validated in this pass -- possible follow-up"]}

